  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.5.0-preview.1 — Final production-readiness polish. No public API changes; no behavior changes.\n\nPositioning:\n  - README leads with an explicit \"Production-ready for owned and trusted\n    ecosystems\" banner above the split-surface maturity table.\n  - \"Roadmap to 1.0\" gates re-framed as external-signal blockers (upstream\n    PostQuantum.Jwt 1.0, IETF JOSE PQC drafts, third-party audit) rather\n    than missing engineering — the version label is conservative on\n    purpose, the code beneath is production-discipline.\n  - SECURITY.md and KNOWN-GAPS.md honesty statements re-aligned to match.\n\nSupply chain:\n  - README's verification section renamed \"How to verify this package\n    (supply chain — three commands)\" so it is easy to find for auditors\n    landing on the page cold.\n  - New docs/SUPPLY-CHAIN.md — auditor-facing companion: chain-of-custody\n    diagram, per-arrow verification table, full release.yml hygiene\n    checklist, reproducibility recipe, SHA-256 cross-check guidance, and\n    a \"what this does NOT prove\" honesty section.\n\nReference samples:\n  - PostQuantum.Identity.Mvc.Demo: token Lifetime lifted into a single\n    TokenConstants.Lifetime source-of-truth; AccountController login and\n    refresh responses now surface expires_in for parity with the\n    minimal-API demo.\n\nRepo hygiene:\n  - .gitignore now explicitly excludes nuget.key / nuget.key.* / *.nuget.key\n    so a stray local API-key file at the repo root can never be committed.\n\nEarlier highlights — 0.3.0 added hardened Argon2id and token KATs, the\nproduction-shaped samples (refresh/logout/JWKS/revocation), opinionated\nwork-factor presets, startup options validation, the preflight logger, and\nthe supply-chain verification flow. 0.2.0 added the PBKDF2→Argon2id\nmigrating hasher, kid rotation, AOT-clean claim path, embedded CycloneDX\nSBOM, CI/release workflows, and benchmarks.\n\nStill preview — NOT independently audited. See KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
